# Active Directory Security Lab

## Overview

This project documents my hands-on practice with Active Directory administration and Windows security monitoring in a virtual lab environment.

The purpose of this lab was to develop foundational skills related to:
- User management
- Authentication
- Group Policy
- Windows event monitoring
- Enterprise security concepts

---

## Lab Environment

### Systems Used
- Windows Server
- Windows 10 Client VM
- VirtualBox

### Tools and Features
- Active Directory Users and Computers
- Group Policy Management
- Windows Event Viewer

---

## Activities Completed

### User and Group Management
Created domain users, security groups, and organizational units.

### Group Policy Configuration
Configured password and account lockout policies.

### Authentication Monitoring
Reviewed Windows login events and failed authentication attempts.

### Windows Security Logging
Analyzed Event Viewer logs related to user authentication and system activity.

---

## Skills Demonstrated

- Active Directory administration
- Windows security fundamentals
- Account policy management
- Authentication monitoring
- Security documentation

---

## Lessons Learned

This lab improved my understanding of:
- Enterprise Windows environments
- Authentication workflows
- User and permission management
- Security event logging
